  "summary": "The feathery, uneven edge characteristic of handmade paper.",
  "description": "Deckle edges feature a soft, irregular outline created when water drains unevenly from the paper mold during formation. This natural edge became a distinctive aesthetic marker for quality handmade paper and was later artificially replicated in industrial production.",
